{
  "_comment": [
    "Cross-language test vectors for the pairing wire format.",
    "Every implementation must reproduce these exactly. A framing bug or an off-by-one",
    "in the code derivation shows up as 'pairing does not work' with nothing to read,",
    "so the two ends are pinned to the same bytes here rather than to prose.",
    "Byte strings are lowercase hex.",
    "ed25519 pins signature interoperability: a signature made on one platform must verify on the other.",
    "pairing_v2 pins the commit-reveal ceremony: commitment = sha256(label || client nonce); code over the sorted keys and both nonces."
  ],
  "frames": [
    {
      "why": "empty control payload — length covers the type byte, so it is 1",
      "type": 0,
      "payload": "",
      "encoded": "0000000100"
    },
    {
      "why": "a control message",
      "type": 0,
      "payload": "7b2274223a2268656c6c6f227d",
      "encoded": "0000000e007b2274223a2268656c6c6f227d"
    },
    {
      "why": "a bulk chunk uses type 1",
      "type": 1,
      "payload": "deadbeef",
      "encoded": "0000000501deadbeef"
    }
  ],
